{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — card-only product template.

  An alternate product template, fetched by the block scripts as
  /products/<handle>?view=ymal-card. It returns one card's markup and nothing
  else: no layout, no header, no footer.

  THIS FILE IS THE ELIGIBILITY GATE. Every block renders through it, so the
  rule is enforced in exactly one place. An ineligible product renders as an
  empty string and the calling script skips it.

  Why the gate is here rather than in JavaScript:

  - it reuses the THEME's own product card, so the block looks native and stays
    that way when the theme changes
  - price, image and availability are read live at fetch time, so a handle
    stored three weeks ago cannot render a stale price
  - the decision needs the live product object, which only Liquid has

  Replace the placeholder markup below with a render of the theme's real card
  snippet. Find it first: most themes have something like
  snippets/card-product.liquid or snippets/product-card.liquid.

    {%- render 'card-product', card_product: product -%}
{%- endcomment -%}

{% layout none %}

{%- comment -%}
  The rule (docs/logic.md §4.1), as the storefront can see it.

  1. available      purchasable right now. Liquid knows this directly.
  2. not *SALE*     markdown. Liquid can read the title, so this is checked
                    here as well as in the metafield - it costs nothing and
                    holds even if the metafield is stale.
  3. eligible       stocked at Bali To Produce, so replenishable rather than
                    fixed. Liquid CANNOT compute this: it sees store-wide
                    inventory totals but never inventory by location. The
                    pipeline publishes it to product.metafields.ymal.eligible
                    (scripts/publish_eligibility.py).

  FAILS CLOSED. A product with no ymal.eligible metafield is not shown. A
  missing metafield means the pipeline has never classified it, and "we have
  not checked" must not render as "fine to show" - that is precisely the Wiser
  failure this project exists to fix. The visible cost is an empty block until
  the publish job has run, which is a problem someone notices.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  `.value`, not the metafield object. `product.metafields.ymal.eligible` is an
  object that EXISTS even when it holds false, so testing it directly is truthy
  for an ineligible product - it would fail open, which is the opposite of what
  this gate is for. `.value` is the boolean, and nil when the metafield is
  absent, which is falsy. That is the fail-closed behaviour.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ymal_eligible = product.metafields.ymal.eligible.value -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Liquid has no boolean operators inside a condition, so the *SALE* test cannot
  be inlined - `contains ... == false` is not valid Liquid. Compute it first.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ymal_is_sale = false -%}
{%- if product.title contains '*SALE*' -%}
  {%- assign ymal_is_sale = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if product.available and ymal_eligible and ymal_is_sale == false -%}

  {%- comment -%} PLACEHOLDER — swap for the theme's own card snippet. {%- endcomment -%}
  <a class="ymal__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
    {%- if product.featured_image -%}
      <img
        class="ymal__image"
        src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 }}"
        alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape }}"
        width="400"
        height="{{ 400 | divided_by: product.featured_image.aspect_ratio | round }}"
        loading="lazy"
      >
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="ymal__name">{{ product.title | escape }}</span>
    <span class="ymal__price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
  </a>
{%- endif -%}
